    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d227">

                <pb facs="0370" n="294" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg294"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.248/112: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dodd</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-03-12T18:00:00+01:00">March 12, 1935—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 12—2:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>46. Interview of Goering<anchor n="28" xml:id="d227-f1"/> with <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Daily Mail</hi> representative chosen as means to
                    announce air program. Reliable sources do not believe its announcement is
                    directly retaliatory against British White Paper<anchor n="29" xml:id="d227-f2"
                    /> but simply publicly indicates completion of a military plan regardless of
                    treaty stipulations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodd</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d227-f1" n="28" xml:id="d227-f1-content">
                <p>Hermann Goering, German Minister for Aviation.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d227-f2" n="29" xml:id="d227-f2-content">
                <p>See British Cmd. 4827: <hi rendition="#italic">Statement Relating to Defense
                        Issued in Connexion With the House of Commons Debate on March 11, 1985</hi>.
                    This command paper was dated March 1, 1935, and apparently was released on March
                    4 in anticipation of the scheduled debate on imperial defense.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
